    "body": "Review of PR #142 (skill step 4: apply outside claims). Not clean. Three problems, all in step 4:\n\n1. **Re-applies and re-replies on every run.** The jq filter only excludes owner/member comments; nothing checks whether a claim was already applied. Today `#61` already has `claimed` and assignee `seelesturm`, and the 6 h window still returns that claim, so each 10-minute `/loop` run would re-add the label and post another \"Claim recorded\" comment for 6 h. Needs a check that the reply is not already on the issue, or that the claimant is not already the assignee.\n\n2. **Window is 6 h, but the staleness rule is 4 h** (AGENTS.md \"Outside contributors' claims count\" and the Claim rule). A claim 4-6 h old with no newer comment is stale and must not be taken as fresh. Use `-4 hours` and drop claims with a newer comment from the claimant.\n\n3. **Skip rule is too narrow.** Step 4 only skips when a newer claim comment from someone else exists. AGENTS.md says never work an issue that carries `claimed` unless its last claim is older than 4 h. Issues claimed by sessions' agents (e.g. `#108`, `#109`, `#112`, `#117`, currently labelled `claimed` with no contributor comment) would be taken over by an outside comment. Skip any issue already carrying `claimed` unless its claim is stale.\n\nThe `gh api` call itself runs and returns the expected rows (checked read-only). The `date` fallback and the `--jq` per-page use are fine. Not approved, not merged.",
