    "body": "Re-review at head 8b6ec97a5ad7a678abe121b9f7f87ee647ce9c5c. Not clean.\n\nStatus of the three points from the earlier review:\n1. Re-apply and re-reply on every run: resolved for the taken path. An already-applied claim (label set, claimant is assignee) is skipped.\n2. 6 h window: resolved. The window is now 4 h.\n3. Skip rule for held issues: partly resolved. Two gaps remain:\n   a. A `claimed` issue with no findable claim comment falls through to \"otherwise\" and is taken over. AGENTS.md only allows takeover when the last claim comment is older than 4 h with no newer comment from the claimant. A missing claim comment should be a skip (or a question to the maintainer), not a takeover.\n   b. The \"held by someone else\" branch says reply once, but there is no check for an existing reply. Each 10-minute tick would post the same \"in progress\" reply for up to 4 h. This is the same bug class as point 1. It needs an idempotency check, for example searching the issue's comments for the held reply before posting.\n\nNew contradiction with AGENTS.md (minor): the search window keeps only claim comments created in the last 4 h. AGENTS.md defines staleness as \"older than 4 hours with no newer comment from the claimant\". A claimant who posted a claim more than 4 h ago and has followed up since is dropped by the window rather than checked. The check should use the claimant's latest comment, not the age of the claim alone.\n\nNot approved, not merged.\n",
